    "exact_utf8_text": "**PASS_IN_SCOPE** \u2014 documentation-only architecture review. No blocking findings.\n\nReviewed commit `1dad476cf8df19b9eee7f92578104f133823085d`, tree `442058a68781c9089ad98262ba77fca2fda10d40`. HEAD is detached and the checkout is clean. The cumulative parent diff adds only the three proposal artifacts; `git diff --check` passes.\n\nThe proposed separation of evidence roles from scheduled network requests addresses a real V4 blocker: V4 requires all 15 provider-purpose mappings, while its production predicate admits only four ECMWF FIELD/INDEX pairs ([V4 validator](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/tools/v11_r09_gate3_launch_v4.py:429), [endpoint coverage](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/tools/v11_r09_gate3_launch_v4.py:557)). The proposal keeps V4\u2019s refusal in force, retains three providers and the 2,713-slot denominator, requires all three FIELD evidence roles, and freezes ranges, dependencies, subset and schedule before review ([proposal](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/docs/V11_GATE3_PRODUCTION_MAPPING_DESIGN_20261003.md:141)). Its rights, identity, provenance, denial-history and clock requirements do not silently qualify a provider ([evidence packet](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/docs/V11_GATE3_PRODUCTION_MAPPING_DESIGN_20261003.md:88)).\n\n**P3, nonblocking traceability:** The [source binding](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/docs/V11_GATE3_PRODUCTION_MAPPING_DESIGN_20261003.sources.json:7) omits direct pins for the file defining `SLOTS` and `SLOT_COUNT` and for the collection protocol defining the fixed window. Add those pins to the later exact amendment\u2019s preservation map; I verified the claims directly in the [launch constants](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/tools/v11_r09_gate3_launch.py:26) and [collection protocol](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/docs/V11_R09_GATE3_COLLECTION_PROTOCOL.md:91).\n\nChecks were offline and read-only: the three current status docs, full candidate diff, baseline source and protocol requirements, all 10 source hashes and lengths, all 34 anchors, design hash and length, 15-row verification table, and denominator calculation. I did not rerun the author\u2019s pytest result. Provider rights, private evidence and live restriction state were outside this review. This verdict accepts the proposal\u2019s **review scope only**; it is no protocol amendment or launch authority. **G3-L remains NO_GO, with zero qualified entries and no provider request** ([checkpoint](/tmp/alpha-v11-gate3-production-mapping-review-1dad476/docs/V11_WORK_CHECKPOINT.md:51)).",
